# Minimum launch checklist

A country or function may proceed only when the accountable leader can confirm:

- The approved tools and prohibited uses are clear;
- Local privacy, employment, regulatory, and consultation requirements are complete;
- The local playbook is available in relevant languages;
- The usage-data charter has been communicated;
- Performance dashboards do not create hidden surveillance;
- Employees have paid or protected learning time;
- Managers have been trained not to equate activity with performance;
- A safe disclosure route exists for prior unauthorized use;
- Sensitive-data restrictions are technically enforced where possible;
- Professional and compliance owners have approved relevant use cases;
- Workforce implications have been explained honestly;
- Human review and accountability are defined;
- Accessibility and non-AI alternatives are available where needed;
- Local support and incident escalation are operational; and
- Employees can raise concerns without retaliation.

## Final policy

The group should mandate **safe capability, approved access, training, and governance**—not blind uniformity or artificial usage volume.

The strongest strategy is one in which the organization can:

- distinguish principled resistance from capability gaps;
- treat covert use as intelligence about policy and workflow failures while enforcing data boundaries;
- protect professional judgment;
- disclose exactly how usage metrics operate;
- separate adoption reporting from performance management;
- address job fears with concrete workforce commitments;
- let local leaders adapt the change approach;
- consult employees and their representatives before surveillance or restructuring decisions; and
- stop or redesign a use case when trust, quality, privacy, or customer protection is at risk.

A mandatory AI rollout becomes sustainable when employees experience the mandate not as a demand to perform enthusiasm, but as a clear, controlled investment in better work—with transparent limits, credible protections, and genuine accountability.
